Egan Arithmites is a half-minotaur wanderer out of [[Geography/Lorandris/index|Lorandris]], a man in his middle years, eight or nine feet tall. His copper skin is crossed with old scars, his black hair is tied back, and his beard is thick and shot with gray. From the waist down he is furred black and stands on cloven hooves, so he goes unshod. He wears a long black overcoat and a black raiment, and carries a long rifle and a sword that is also a gun. He follows [[Divinity/Outer Gods/The Compelled|the Compelled]], whose raiment is silver, and no one has said why his is not.

He captained a ship out of Lorandris until a song came into his head and into the heads of his crew. They sold the ship and turned inward, and the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]] gathered them onto the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], where he passed out pamphlets and small stones marked with a trumpet and woke only now and then to what was happening around him. When the strider walked, the song loosened its hold and he came back to himself; when it stopped, the song grew loud again. One of the crewmates he came in with has grown mandibles. He climbed to the surface by an elevator shaft beneath the crater where [[Org/Verdant Holdings/index|Verdant Holdings]] used to stand, meaning to find a way off the strider.

He has carried a bone-carved necklace since before any of this, found at a convocation, a meeting of pirate crews in Lorandrian waters. Black smoke gathers into many hands inside it and pulls at his face, and he blames it for his trouble. [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] reads the necklace as one of the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/index|Ashen Pact]], if not more than one.

He has thrown in with the Party, and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] means to study the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] song in him.
